                <pb facs="0742" n="592" xml:id="pg592"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 1012/–4.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to Chargé Brown.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1906-09-18"><hi rendition="#italic">September 18,
                            1906</hi>.</date></dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 293.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to acknowledge the receipt of your
                    dispatch No. 441, of the 29th ultimo, transmitting correspondence relating to
                    the imprisonment of Ramon Chan.</p>
                <p>It would appear that the Chinese nationality of Mr. Ramon Chan had not been
                    positively ascertained, hut had been inferred from his name.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Alvey A. Adee.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
